    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12393331/comment/12590197",
          "id": "12590197",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=efranqueiro",
            "name": "efranqueiro",
            "key": "efranqueiro",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Esteban Franqueiro",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I'm working on this refactoring and I ended up with an empty Oracle10R2FileSystem. From a code point of view this class should be removed, but from a user's perspective, I think its more clear to have a class with a more accurate name.\nThe other possibility is to rename the already mentioned OracleBaseFaileSystem as Oracle10R2FileSystem, and make OracleFileSystem inheriit from it. I don't like this either.\nWDYYT?\nRegards,\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=efranqueiro",
            "name": "efranqueiro",
            "key": "efranqueiro",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Esteban Franqueiro",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-04-17T20:31:31.724+0000",
          "updated": "2008-04-17T20:31:31.724+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12393331/comment/12590494",
          "id": "12590494",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=efranqueiro",
            "name": "efranqueiro",
            "key": "efranqueiro",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Esteban Franqueiro",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Is it worth doing this work for the Oracle DB Persistence Managers (not the bundle PMs) too?\nThe bundle PMs for Oracle already support 10.2+, but there's a name mismatch because there's an Oracle9PM, and OraclePM is for 10+.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=efranqueiro",
            "name": "efranqueiro",
            "key": "efranqueiro",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Esteban Franqueiro",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2008-04-18T15:55:45.575+0000",
          "updated": "2008-04-18T15:55:45.575+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12393331/comment/12590506",
          "id": "12590506",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Hi,\nI don't know how much it is used. I would deprecate those persistence managers soon, as they are much slower then the bundle persistence managers. So in my view it doesn't make sense to work on non-bundle persistence managers any more.\nRegards,\nThomas",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
